Okay, here’s a short story first:

Pipkin Sprocketbottom, a particularly fussy gnome warlock, adjusted his spectacles and glared at the dense foliage of Stranglethorn Vale. “Honestly, this jungle is *dreadful* for a gentleman’s questing,” he muttered, swatting at a particularly persistent mosquito. His Succubus, Lilith (a surprisingly grumpy name for a demonic entity), clung to his shoulder, occasionally emitting a low, unsettling giggle. 

“Are you *sure* this is the right path, Pipkin?” Lilith hissed, her eyes glowing faintly. “I’m detecting a significant concentration of…shiny things. And a rather large, grumpy boar.”

Pipkin consulted his map, a miniature parchment rolled up with a tiny quill. “The rumors speak of a lost artifact, a shimmering shard of solidified shadow. It’s said to be guarded by a beast of considerable size. And, of course, infested with… unpleasant creatures.” He shuddered dramatically. Lilith promptly launched herself into the air, a whirlwind of crimson and shadow, heading straight for the boar. Pipkin sighed. “Just… try not to get us killed, darling.”



---

**Answer:**

Voidwalkers grant increased pet health. [end of text]


